  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5a\"><p><strong>5a</strong></p><p> </p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_03\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 3\" src=\"asset:fig_03\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p> </p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5b\"><p><strong>5b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>The force on the point mass due to a <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2M\"></span> mass is twice the force due to a <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> mass. </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_04\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 4\" src=\"asset:fig_04\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Therefore the force exerted on the point mass is equal to the force exerted by two <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> masses placed at the two right-hand side corners of the square.</p>\n<p>Distance between D and a corner of the square: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\sqrt{6.3^{2}+6.3^{2}}}{2} \\approx 4.45 \\: \\mu\"></span>m</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F = 2 \\times (6.67 \\times 10^{-11}) \\times \\frac{(5.8 \\times 10^{4})(0.786)}{\\left ( 4.45 \\times 10^{-6} \\right )^{2}} \\times cos(45^{\\circ}) \\approx 2.2 \\times 10^{5}\"></span> N</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5c\"><p><strong>5c</strong></p><p></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a = \\frac{2.2 \\times 10^{5}}{0.786} \\approx 2.8 \\times 10^{5}\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span></p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5d\"><p><strong>5d</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>When the point mass is released, a force acts on the point mass horizontally to the left, along the line that passes through the midpoint between the two <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> masses.</p>\n<p>This force is proportional to and opposite the displacement from the midpoint between the two <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> masses, so the point mass oscillates with simple harmonic motion.</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Four point masses are located at the vertices of a square of side length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.3 \\: \\mu\"></span>m. Point D is at the centre of the square.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>a. Draw an arrow on the diagram to represent the direction of the gravitational field at D.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>\n<p>A point mass of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"786\"></span> g is placed at D. <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M = 5.8 \\times 10^{4}\"></span> kg.</p>\n<p>b. Determine the magnitude of the net force that acts on the point mass at D.</p>\n<p>   [3]</p>\n<p>The two <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2M\"></span> masses are removed and the point mass at D is released.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n\n<p>c. Find the initial acceleration of the point mass.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>\n<p>d. Outline the subsequent motion of the point mass.</p>\n<p>   [2]</p>"
  },
